import pathlib,json,hashlib,datetime
D=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];rows=json.loads((D/'extracted.json').read_text())
notes={
367410:('parked_asymptotic_structural','Conjecture 2; Theorem 3 and Lemma 4; f(n,k)=max(n0*n1+floor((k-1)*n0/2)).','Literal quantifier is sufficiently large n depending on T, not every finite n. The balanced-tree theorem also assumes Erdos-Sos for subtrees. Small graph violations cannot refute eventual scope. The exact missing ingredient is the tree decomposition Lemma 4 for arbitrary unbalanced T (or an independent infinite extremal family).','No numerical sweep: finite n cannot resolve the eventual bound. Source concluding remarks and conditional theorem inspected; 2026 balanced spectral follow-up found, not a solution of arbitrary-tree bound.'),
367548:('parked_unboundedness','Conjecture 16; Proposition 6; Theorem 9.','One needs a uniform transfer of separating saturated families in the unbounded direction, and a bounded saturation witness construction for arbitrary bounded factors in the converse. Theorem 9 uses special posets and a hypercube condition unavailable in general. No short combination of the inspected source lemmas closes the missing cases.','No finite saturation sweep: any finite collection of sat(n,P) values fails to certify unboundedness. Current arXiv body and 2026 published Conjecture 16 search evidence retain the problem; older arXiv bodies not all compared.'),
367636:('parked_analytic','Conjecture 3.7 after Theorems 3.5 and 3.6.','Needs a spectral characterization in the boundary-zero weight case for elliptic/double-parabolic dynamics. The zero-free case is already described; using a hyperbolic example would violate the source hypotheses. No finite exact certificate route was found.','No numerical search; spectra and accumulation points are not finite decidable data. Exact conjecture and immediate spectral context read, not a complete proof audit of operator theory.'),
367655:('excluded_known_source_refutation','Current source Theorem 6 (Pruesse-Ruskey non-simple Venn arrangements); all four arXiv versions downloaded.','The source itself constructs non-simple counterexamples for every n>=4 with even order and no perfect matching. The Hamilton cycle obstruction is already the published result, rather than a new conjecture.','No search needed. Actual theorem/counterexample passage read; SoCG 2026 source located. No reuse/modification of printed Figure 6 attempted.'),
367774:('parked_unbounded_class','Linear-forest conjecture in self-chi-guarding section; stars and P4-free cases established.','The target means every fixed k-fold graph-intersection is chi-bounded. A finite graph with large chromatic number cannot alone refute existence of an arbitrary binding function. Need a fixed linear forest H and fixed k with a bounded-clique, unbounded-chromatic intersection family, or a uniform binding theorem.','No misleading small finite sweep. Source definition and necessary-condition framework read; Chaniotis thesis Conjecture 8.7 and neighboring cases located. No all-citing-work clearance.'),
367788:('parked_rationality','Few-monochromatic Conjecture 5.8 in v2 (numbering differs in v1); coefficient U[n,i,j].','For each fixed i,j the claimed rational function has no prescribed degree bound. Any finite list of normalized coefficients admits a rational polynomial interpolant, so finite computation cannot falsify this quantifier. Need an all-genus recurrence/potential proving rationality, or a genuine nonrational sequence proof.','Both arXiv versions downloaded; distinct many-monochromatic conjecture not substituted. Source PDE/recurrence discussion explains why its available induction is not directly a proof of the few-monochromatic claim. No source-formula evaluation reported as a result.'),
367789:('excluded_known_source_theorem','Banerjee-Chakraborty-Das-Paul, A spanning tree model for chromatic homology; theorem labelled Conjecture 25 [HGPR06], Section 4.2 proof.','The source states and proves the reserved existence/divisibility-of-torsion claim. The general construction uses spanning-tree classes and then block decomposition/Kunneth; converse uses loop vanishing and tree torsion-freeness. This cannot earn new credit.','Both arXiv versions downloaded, including v2 dated 2026-10-27. Target statement and Section 4.2 ending read; no independent homology computation or Lean replay claimed.'),
367794:('excluded_published_strengthening','Fox-Tidor, SoCG 2026, Corollaries 3.8 and 3.9, PDF pp. 9-10.','Corollary 3.9 explicitly strengthens Davies-Georgakopoulos-Hatzel-McCarty Conjecture 20: K[t,t]-free sphere intersection graphs in R^d have O_d(t^(1/d)*n^(1-1/d)) separators. Their proof combines the separator theorem and linear edge bound. This implies the reserved weaker exponent for d>=2; the source already supplies d=1.','Downloaded the primary PDF and read the corollary and its precursor bootstrap proof. No claim that arbitrary CDC or an unrelated separator theorem solves this target.'),
367832:('excluded_known_source_theorem','Dovgoshey-Cantor-Rovenska, Theorem 4.3; Conjecture 3.1 is recalled historically.','Theorem 4.3 states the exact finite four-point obstruction characterization, and more (spaces with limit points). Its proof is in the source. Also MathDB paraphrases weak similarity as rescaling; the source order-isomorphism definition must control any formal endpoint. No correction is proposed as new mathematics.','Theorem statement and adjacent proof read. No new ultrametric enumeration needed; infinite Conjecture 6.1 is a different, unreserved scope.'),
367984:('parked_after_exact_sampling','Conjecture 5 and Theorem 10; authors verified all source candidates through 28 vertices.','Five independently sampled triangulated spheres of orders 30,30,32,36,40, each with minimum degree 5 and no separating triangle, gave only 4-colourable additions. Need a non-4-colourable crossing addition with no internal degree-4 vertex, or a full structural proof. Sampling is not canonical coverage.','474 raw edge-crossing additions tested by SAT (84+84+90+102+114). Models checked against every CNF clause; sphere Euler/link checks performed. Generator uses classical edge splits/flips rather than augmenting a printed obstruction. See outputs/onecrossing*.json and outputs/sat-verification.json.'),
368114:('parked_after_sustained_exact_search','Christoph et al., Conjecture 5.4; Anastos-Fabian-Muyesser-Szabo original Conjecture 1.3 / Remark 2.','No independent obstruction survived. Complete connected-union searches at orders 12 and 14, partial order 16, and random samples through order 24 found all requested n-1 colour profiles. Disconnected unions with K4 blocks remain in literal scope; constructions obtained by switching/padding the printed K4 obstruction are excluded and were not promoted.','All versions of the 2025 paper and original 2212.03100 downloaded. Exact search fixes M1 and classifies M1 union M2 by even cycle lengths, then enumerates every disjoint M3. N=12: 13310 M3, 13166 connected. N=14: 176766 M3, 175641 connected. N=16: first cycle type [2,2,2,2], 435158 M3, 423447 connected; stopped at 100 seconds, not complete. Random counts in matching-search.json; no hit.'),
368164:('parked_major_equivalence','Mazzuoccolo-Mkrtchyan Conjecture 5; Hakobyan-Mkrtchyan equivalence.','Equivalent to the stronger 5-cycle-double-cover conjecture. The ordinary cycle-double-cover theorem does not bound the number of even subgraphs by five. A 2026 follow-up proves five perfect matchings suffice and four cover 299/315 of edges, not four-coverability.','Source equivalence read; Zhou-Wang 2610.01137 primary body read. Zerafa 2609.28118 abstract located but HTML conversion unavailable, recorded. No general proof/counterexample, and no purported finite small-graph result substituted for the equivalence.'),
368169:('parked_major_equivalence','Source comparison of 3/5 and 2/5 bounds in the 5-CDC discussion.','The 2/5 lower bound follows from averaging a five-member double cover (total length 2|E|); that routine implication is not the conjectured 3/5 strengthening. Need a universal transformation that raises a member to 3|E|/5, or a rigorous separation of the two universal assertions.','No heavy search: a finite graph failing the stronger cover condition would require simultaneously certifying exact even-subgraph semantics and nonexistence of all covers, while it would not by itself establish the logical relation between the two universal conjectures. Source bound/equivalence passage read; no solution claimed.'),
368265:('parked_after_structured_surface_search','A census of face-transitive surfaces, Conjecture 6.2 and classification discussion.','No face-transitive member in ten twisted triangular-grid quotients: (m,n)=(4,4),(5,6),(7,8),(17,41),(23,31), shifts 0,1. The last two have 1394 and 1426 faces, beyond the census face limit 1280. This structured family is not all simplicial Klein bottles. A proof needs a global classification or flat-cover normalizer argument valid for every valence type.','Automorphism candidates propagated from every oriented image of a base face. Exact face orbit sizes saved; not a Lean-certified topological classification. Printed equivelar examples already have multiple face orbits; no small alteration of them offered as a candidate.'),
368277:('parked_generic_geometric','Himmelmann-Schulze-Winter Conjecture 1.1 and genericity framework; d=3 theorem.','A flexible special realization such as a regular cube is not a counterexample to generic rigidity. Need a type whose generic realization component has deficient rank under edge-length and coplanarity constraints. No finite independent type/rank certificate found.','All three source arXiv versions downloaded. July 2026 follow-up 2607.09252 explicitly says higher-dimensional generic rigidity remains open; inspected introductory scope, not full realization-space proofs.'),
368314:('excluded_prior_public_lean_refutation','Omega D5/S3/Combinatorics/Geometry/IntervalClosedSignedCardinalityRefutation.result; commit 58ecb855708155edd05871ad8141f748de45237b dated 2026-10-04.','Independent search reproduced a 73-state orbit on [3]x[12], initial rows {6,...,11}, {5}, empty, with signed sum +1. This is the sign-paired counterpart of the public exact 73-state refutation. It is already Lean-proved and excluded; no new Lean endpoint attempted.','Full exact enumerations at n=4,6,8,10 had all sums zero. At n=12 enumeration stops on first failure. Separate full-interval Python toggle checker verifies all 73 states, closure, distinctness, convexity and nonzero sum. Current public body and quantified claim read after the exact search; initial broad path query missed the SignedCardinality keyword. Subsequent targeted search found the prior result before formalization.'),
368382:('parked_after_constructive_sat','Colbourn Conjecture 1.7 in arXiv2505.07252; rational-outline sections and source theorem h1<=3*hmin.','Six full Latin squares realizing partitions in the bound were constructed and independently verified. These are parameter instances, not a proof of the all-partitions statement. A general rational outline followed by a common dilation proves only a scaled realization and does not settle the literal undilated RP.','SAT witnesses: (4,2,2,1,1,1), (4,3,2,1,1,1), (4,4,3,2,1,1), (4,4,4,3,2,1), (5,4,3,2,1,1,1), (6,5,3,2,1,1,1,1), orders 11,12,15,18,17,20. All row/column and disjoint subsquare constraints checked directly, plus all CNF clauses. No finite witness credited.'),
368492:('excluded_prior_public_lean_refutation','Lean Pool CommonNeighbourConjecture; SaxlCounterexamples.MainTheorems.mainTheorem.','Public theorem gives, for every B>=2 and every degree bound, a finite faithful primitive group of base size B with two nonadjacent points having no common neighbour. Generalized Saxl edges are pairs contained in minimum bases, precisely the 2-section of the source Saxl hypergraph. This already refutes the reserved universal claim, including primitive scope.','Lean Pool HEAD 01db1d7049cf9668bda1e9e106875ee1278b43e6, projects.yml source alunik/common-neighbour-conjecture commit b2c0a8f95aa4dca76a034a0e769a8c8249f38ae2. Entry, actual Examples/MainTheorems.lean and Saxl/Generalized.lean definitions read; no replay claimed.'),
368836:('parked_after_exact_graph_search','Hoang Conjecture 1.2; Theorems 1.4 and 1.5; Figure 1 correcting Dong-Xu-Yu argument.','Every atlas graph through order 7 and every tested random graph through order 13 was perfectly divisible; no MNPD clique-cutset violation found. The invalid published proof cannot be repaired merely by taking A1 union A2: clique-cutset vertices assigned differently can create an odd hole on one side. Need a compatible perfect maximum-clique transversal extension, or an independent MNPD witness.','Exact hereditary chi/omega/perfect-division DP on all 1253 atlas graphs; random G(n,p), p=.2,.4,.6,.8, seed221, counts in divisibility-random.json. Source proof body and corrected construction read, two source versions downloaded; no modification of Figure 1 used.'),
368837:('parked_after_exact_graph_search','Hoang Conjecture 4.2; Chudnovsky-Sivaraman bull-free result and Song-Xu banner-free result.','No P5-free non-perfectly-divisible witness in exact atlas or bounded random search. Related bull-free/banner-free theorems are proper subclasses; P5-free MNPD having no clique cutset is a reduction, not a proof that no such atom exists. Need a new decomposition for remaining P5-free atoms or an independent finite obstruction.','Exact hereditary DP and direct induced P5 test. All 1253 atlas graphs are PD. Random sample P5-free counts through order13 recorded; selected 2017/2024 primary PDFs downloaded and theorem scope read. No full current MathDB status or all-citing-body clearance claimed.')}
results={}
for key,o in rows.items():
 i=int(key);outcome,loc,math,attempt=notes[i];a=o['source_url'].split('/')[-1];receipts=[]
 for p in sorted((D/'sources').glob(a+'*.receipt.json')):receipts.append({'path':str(p.relative_to(D)),**{k:v for k,v in json.loads(p.read_text()).items() if k in ['url','utc','status','sha256','error','challenge']}})
 results[key]={'mathdb_id':i,'title':o['title'],'literal_statement':o['statement'],'source_url':o['source_url'],'provenance':o['provenance'],'outcome':outcome,'credit':0,'review_depth':'literal_statement_and_primary_target_context; depth is detailed in attempts, not an all-paper audit','source_locator':loc,'mathematical_disposition_and_remaining_gap':math,'attempts_and_coverage':attempt,'historical_checks':'outputs/history-full.json; current ledger read-only; protected/excluded families in TASK respected','registry_screen':'outputs/registry-screen.json; positive bodies inspected, no general absence claim','source_receipts':receipts,'lean_endpoint':None,'qualification':'Excluded or parked; root acceptance not requested. Numerical data are diagnostics.'}
assert len(results)==20 and set(map(int,results))==set(json.loads((D/'reservation.json').read_text())['ids'])
(D/'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(results,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
